{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "We evaluate on two 7B-parameter models sharing the Qwen2 backbone (28 layers, 28 heads, 4-group GQA): \textbf{DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B}~\cite{deepseek-r1-2025}, distilled from DeepSeek-R1 with explicit chain-of-thought traces yielding pronounced phase structure; and \textbf{Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct}~\cite{qwen25-2024}, with standard instruction tuning, providing a cross-model replication target. Both are loaded in \texttt{bfloat16} with eager attention.\footnote{An earlier \texttt{float16} configuration produced sporadic NaN values; \texttt{bfloat16} eliminated all occurrences.}
We use 50 problems stratified from MATH-500~\cite{math500-neurips2021}, sampling uniformly across categories with a fixed seed. Each problem is decoded greedily (\texttt{max\_new\_tokens}$=$2048).
All confidence intervals and significance tests use nonparametric bootstrap ($B{=}10{,}000$)~\cite{efron-1993}. Paired bootstrap controls for problem-level variance. All tests yield $p_{\text{Bonf}} < 0.005$ at every sparsity level.\footnote{Experiments on 4$\times$ NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 96\,GB GPUs.}
